IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-art9-restricted-section`
IMPORT `g3-art10-public-access`
IMPORT `ind-a-tests-fixtures`

-- ind-a-tests-art8-10.l4: independent tests of Articles 8 to 10 (the register, the restricted section, public access).
-- Expected values from WORK/ind-a/expectations.md (S8.x, S9.x, S10.x). The Commissioner's satisfaction and consideration are supplied as stated inputs.

§ `ind-a tests: Articles 8 to 10`

§§ `Helpers`

`ind-a R` MEANS `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
    `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
    `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
    `reach of Article 10(4)` IS `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
    `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
    `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
    `day on which an entry takes effect` IS `on the day of the entry`
    `the most recent year` IS `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
    `required steps notices noted` IS `every notice that has been served`
    `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
    `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
    `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
    `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
    `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`

-- The same, with the day of the event counted (F3.4 second reading), with the rolling 29 February (F3.5 second reading), with the ten years from deregistration (F3.1 second reading),
-- and with "was registered in the general section" read as ever (F3.11 second reading).
`ind-a R count day of event` MEANS `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
    `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
    `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
    `reach of Article 10(4)` IS `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
    `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS `the day of the event is the first day, so the last day of the period is the day before the anniversary`
    `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
    `day on which an entry takes effect` IS `on the day of the entry`
    `the most recent year` IS `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
    `required steps notices noted` IS `every notice that has been served`
    `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
    `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
    `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
    `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
    `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`

`ind-a R roll 29 February` MEANS `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
    `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
    `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
    `reach of Article 10(4)` IS `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
    `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
    `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS `the date rolls forward into the next month`
    `day on which an entry takes effect` IS `on the day of the entry`
    `the most recent year` IS `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
    `required steps notices noted` IS `every notice that has been served`
    `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
    `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
    `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
    `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
    `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`

`ind-a R from deregistration` MEANS `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
    `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the charity is deregistered`
    `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
    `reach of Article 10(4)` IS `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
    `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
    `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
    `day on which an entry takes effect` IS `on the day of the entry`
    `the most recent year` IS `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
    `required steps notices noted` IS `every notice that has been served`
    `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
    `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
    `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
    `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
    `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`

`ind-a R ever general` MEANS `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
    `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
    `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS `the calendar year`
    `reach of Article 10(4)` IS `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
    `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
    `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
    `day on which an entry takes effect` IS `on the day of the entry`
    `the most recent year` IS `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
    `required steps notices noted` IS `every notice that has been served`
    `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
    `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
    `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS `any section the entity was ever entered in`
    `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
    `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`

GIVEN st IS A `Standing on the register`
      ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
GIVETH AN Entity
`ind-a charity entity` st ks MEANS
    `ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey" st ks TRUE (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`) (LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`)

GIVEN st IS A `Standing on the register`
      ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      orc IS A BOOLEAN
      dereg IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Registered charity`
`ind-a registered charity` st ks orc dereg MEANS
    `Registered charity` WITH
        entity IS `ind-a charity entity` st ks
        `registration number` IS "JC-0042"
        `registered name` IS "Hope Jersey"
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date deregistered` IS dereg
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "the prevention or relief of poverty"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "relief of poverty in Jersey by a food bank"
        `is an organized religious charity` IS orc

`ind-a general company charity` MEANS `ind-a registered charity` `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`) FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN premises IS A LIST OF `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
      prev IS A LIST OF STRING
      nInfo IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
`ind-a 8(3) facts` premises prev nInfo MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` WITH
        `other premises` IS premises
        `principal address entered` IS JUST "1 Bond Street, St Helier"
        `previous registered names` IS prev
        `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)` IS nInfo

GIVEN addr IS A STRING, dwelling IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
`ind-a premises` addr dwelling MEANS
    `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))` WITH
        address IS addr
        `in Jersey` IS TRUE
        `a private dwelling house` IS dwelling
        `at or from which the charity undertakes an activity` IS TRUE

`ind-a plain 8(3) facts` MEANS `ind-a 8(3) facts` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

`ind-a RSN on the charity` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
        `date served` IS YMD 2025 3 1
        `steps to be taken by` IS JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS TRUE

`ind-a RSN on a governor` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `a governor of the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`
        `date served` IS YMD 2025 4 1
        `steps to be taken by` IS NOTHING
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS FALSE

GIVEN rc IS A `Registered charity`
      by53 IS A BOOLEAN
      rsns IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
      o139 IS A BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
`ind-a entries` rc by53 rsns o139 facts MEANS `Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` `ind-a R` rc by53 rsns o139 facts

`ind-a core entries` MEANS LIST `a note of the status of the entity`, `the names of each of the governors`, `the principal address`, `the registered charitable purposes`, `the registered public benefit statement`, `the date on which the charity was registered`, `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`

GIVEN ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A `Requirement of the note of status (Article 8(3)(a))`
`ind-a note for` ks MEANS `Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` `ind-a R` (`ind-a charity entity` `entered in the general section` ks)

GIVEN req IS A BOOLEAN, office IS A MAYBE STRING, main IS A MAYBE `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`, govAddrs IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
`ind-a address facts` req office main govAddrs MEANS
    `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH
        `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS req
        `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS office
        `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS main
        `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS govAddrs

GIVEN ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`ind-a principal addresses` ks facts MEANS `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `ind-a R` (`ind-a charity entity` `an applicant for registration` ks) facts

§§ `Article 8(3) (S8.3-01 to S8.3m-01)`

-- S8.3-01 a general-section Jersey company, nothing special -> the core items, and (d) only with other premises (src:222-238)
#ASSERT `ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts` EQUALS `ind-a core entries`
#ASSERT elem `the address of any other premises in Jersey` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE (`ind-a 8(3) facts` (LIST `ind-a premises` "Shop, 5 King Street, St Helier" FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY))
-- S8.3-01 not required for that charity: (h), (i), (k), (l), (m)
#ASSERT NOT elem `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
#ASSERT NOT elem `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
#ASSERT NOT elem `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
#ASSERT NOT elem `the previous registered names` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
#ASSERT NOT elem `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
-- S8.3-01 a restricted-section charity: the same items are entered (src:222 "whether entered in the general or restricted section")
#ASSERT `ind-a entries` (`ind-a registered charity` `entered in the restricted section` (LIST `a company`) FALSE NOTHING) FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts` EQUALS `ind-a core entries`
-- S8.3a-01 an (e) body -> details of the enactment / Act / Charter required (src:225)
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
-- S8.3a-02 (g), (h), (j) -> details required (src:225)
#ASSERT NOT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
#ASSERT NOT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
#ASSERT NOT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
-- S8.3a-03 (a), (b), (ba), (c), (d), (f), (i) -> no details required (src:225)
#ASSERT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
#ASSERT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
#ASSERT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
#ASSERT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
#ASSERT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `a foundation`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
#ASSERT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `a company`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
#ASSERT null ((`ind-a note for` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`)
-- S8.3a-04 the "also within (a)?" note: required for (f) to (j), not for (a) to (e) or (ba) (src:224)
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `a company`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `a foundation`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- S8.3a-05 a Jersey company that is a trustee -> "(f), also within (a)" (src:224)
#ASSERT (`ind-a note for` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- S8.3d-01 a shop is entered; a governor's private dwelling house is not (src:228)
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` (`ind-a 8(3) facts` (LIST `ind-a premises` "Shop, 5 King Street, St Helier" FALSE, `ind-a premises` "Governor's home, La Rue, St Ouen" TRUE) EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS LIST "Shop, 5 King Street, St Helier"
-- S8.3h-01 an organized religious charity -> (h) (src:232)
#ASSERT elem `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity` (`ind-a entries` (`ind-a registered charity` `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`) TRUE NOTHING) FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
-- S8.3i-01 meets the test by virtue of a 5(3) Order -> (i) (src:233)
#ASSERT elem `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` TRUE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
-- S8.3j-01 (j) is entered whether or not the return was sent (src:234)
#ASSERT elem `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
-- S8.3k-01 an RSN served on the charity, or on a governor -> (k) (src:235)
#ASSERT elem `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE (LIST `ind-a RSN on the charity`) FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
#ASSERT elem `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE (LIST `ind-a RSN on a governor`) FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
-- S8.3l-01 renamed from X -> previous name entered (src:236)
#ASSERT elem `the previous registered names` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE (`ind-a 8(3) facts` EMPTY (LIST "Hope for Jersey") EMPTY))
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(l) the previous registered names to be entered` (`ind-a 8(3) facts` EMPTY (LIST "Hope for Jersey") EMPTY) EQUALS LIST "Hope for Jersey"
-- S8.3m-01 an Order under 13(9)(c) applies -> (m) (src:237)
#ASSERT elem `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY TRUE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)
-- S8.3n-01 other information prescribed by Order -> (n) (src:238)
#ASSERT elem `other information prescribed by the Minister by Order` (`ind-a entries` `ind-a general company charity` FALSE EMPTY FALSE (`ind-a 8(3) facts` EMPTY EMPTY (LIST "the charity's website address")))
-- S8.1-01 the Commissioner must establish and maintain a register (src:217)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(1) the Commissioner must establish and maintain a register of charities` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `establish and maintain a register of charities` AT 1
-- a formerly registered charity in the historic section has no 8(3) entries (src:222 "each registered charity")
#ASSERT null (`ind-a entries` (`ind-a registered charity` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` (LIST `a company`) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2024 1 1))) FALSE EMPTY FALSE `ind-a plain 8(3) facts`)

§§ `Article 8(4) (S8.4-01 to S8.4-07)`

-- S8.4-01 a company -> its registered office (src:240)
#ASSERT `ind-a principal addresses` (LIST `a company`) (`ind-a address facts` TRUE (JUST "1 Bond Street, St Helier") NOTHING (LIST "La Rue, St Ouen")) EQUALS LIST "1 Bond Street, St Helier"
-- S8.4-02 a foundation -> its registered office or business address (src:240)
#ASSERT `ind-a principal addresses` (LIST `a foundation`) (`ind-a address facts` TRUE (JUST "2 Hill Street, St Helier") NOTHING EMPTY) EQUALS LIST "2 Hill Street, St Helier"
-- S8.4-03 another entity its constitutional Law requires to have a Jersey registered office -> that address (src:240)
#ASSERT `ind-a principal addresses` (LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`) (`ind-a address facts` TRUE (JUST "3 Mulcaster Street, St Helier") NOTHING EMPTY) EQUALS LIST "3 Mulcaster Street, St Helier"
-- S8.4-04 a trust not so required, managed from an office in St Helier -> that office (src:241)
#ASSERT `ind-a principal addresses` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`) (`ind-a address facts` FALSE NOTHING (JUST (`ind-a premises` "Office, 4 Library Place, St Helier" FALSE)) (LIST "La Rue, St Ouen")) EQUALS LIST "Office, 4 Library Place, St Helier"
-- S8.4-05 only premises a governor's private dwelling -> (c) a governor's Jersey address (src:241-242)
#ASSERT `ind-a principal addresses` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) (`ind-a address facts` FALSE NOTHING (JUST (`ind-a premises` "La Rue, St Ouen" TRUE)) (LIST "La Rue, St Ouen")) EQUALS LIST "La Rue, St Ouen"
-- S8.4-06 no Jersey premises, one governor with a Jersey address -> that address (src:242)
#ASSERT `ind-a principal addresses` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) (`ind-a address facts` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (LIST "Le Mont, Trinity")) EQUALS LIST "Le Mont, Trinity"
-- S8.4-07 a foreign entity with no Jersey premises and no governor with a Jersey address -> no principal address in Jersey (src:239-242)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` `ind-a R` (`ind-a charity entity` `an applicant for registration` (LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`)) (`ind-a address facts` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)

§§ `Article 8(5) (S8.5-01 to S8.5-04)`

GIVEN placements IS A LIST OF `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
      prev IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)`
`ind-a 8(5) facts` placements prev MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` WITH
        `placements of the entity before deregistration` IS placements
        `previous registered names` IS prev
        `matters prescribed by an Order under Article 8(5)(e)` IS EMPTY

GIVEN s IS A `Section of the register`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
`ind-a placed` s d MEANS `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` WITH `the section` IS s, `date of the entry` IS d

`ind-a deregistered charity` MEANS `ind-a registered charity` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` (LIST `a company`) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2023 6 30))

-- S8.5-01 a general-section charity deregistered: number, names, reason, dates (src:243-247)
#ASSERT `Art 8(5) the entries required in the historic section` `ind-a R` `ind-a deregistered charity` (`ind-a 8(5) facts` (LIST `ind-a placed` `the general section` (YMD 2019 3 1)) (LIST "Hope for Jersey")) EQUALS LIST `the entity's former registered number`, `the name under which the entity was registered immediately before deregistration, and the names under which it was previously so registered`, `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`, `the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered`
#ASSERT `Art 8(5)(b) the names to be entered in the historic section` `ind-a R` `ind-a deregistered charity` (`ind-a 8(5) facts` (LIST `ind-a placed` `the general section` (YMD 2019 3 1)) (LIST "Hope for Jersey")) EQUALS LIST "Hope Jersey", "Hope for Jersey"
-- S8.5-02 restricted throughout -> no name (src:245)
#ASSERT `Art 8(5) the entries required in the historic section` `ind-a R` `ind-a deregistered charity` (`ind-a 8(5) facts` (LIST `ind-a placed` `the restricted section` (YMD 2019 3 1)) EMPTY) EQUALS LIST `the entity's former registered number`, `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`, `the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered`
#ASSERT null (`Art 8(5)(b) the names to be entered in the historic section` `ind-a R` `ind-a deregistered charity` (`ind-a 8(5) facts` (LIST `ind-a placed` `the restricted section` (YMD 2019 3 1)) EMPTY))
-- S8.5-03 deregistered for failing to comply with an RSN -> the RSN's reason is summarised; otherwise not required (src:246)
#ASSERT `Art 8(5)(c) the summary must include the reason for the service of the notice` `the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(5)(c) the summary must include the reason for the service of the notice` `on the entity's own application under Article 15`
-- S8.5-04 general 2019, restricted 2020, deregistered 2023 (AMBIG-6): my reading -> no name; the other reading -> names
#ASSERT null (`Art 8(5)(b) the names to be entered in the historic section` `ind-a R` `ind-a deregistered charity` (`ind-a 8(5) facts` (LIST `ind-a placed` `the general section` (YMD 2019 3 1), `ind-a placed` `the restricted section` (YMD 2020 6 1)) EMPTY))
#ASSERT NOT null (`Art 8(5)(b) the names to be entered in the historic section` `ind-a R ever general` `ind-a deregistered charity` (`ind-a 8(5) facts` (LIST `ind-a placed` `the general section` (YMD 2019 3 1), `ind-a placed` `the restricted section` (YMD 2020 6 1)) EMPTY))

§§ `Article 8(6) (S8.6-02 to S8.6-04)`

GIVEN k IS A `Document of a kind within Article 8(6)`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))`
`ind-a copy` k d MEANS `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH kind IS k, `date received or made` IS d, `date it ceased to be operative` IS NOTHING

-- S8.6-02 a constitution copy received 2020-03-15: event day not counted -> may be discarded from 2030-03-16; event day counted -> from 2030-03-15 (src:249)
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a R` (`ind-a copy` `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it` (YMD 2020 3 15)) `ind-a general company charity` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2030 3 16)
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a R count day of event` (`ind-a copy` `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it` (YMD 2020 3 15)) `ind-a general company charity` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2030 3 15)
-- S8.6-02 ten years from deregistration: while the charity is registered the copy is kept
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a R from deregistration` (`ind-a copy` `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it` (YMD 2020 3 15)) `ind-a general company charity` EQUALS `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`
-- S8.6-03 a copy received 2020-02-29: last day 2030-02-28 (clip) -> discard from 2030-03-01; last day 2030-03-01 (roll) -> from 2030-03-02
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a R` (`ind-a copy` `an annual return of the charity` (YMD 2020 2 29)) `ind-a general company charity` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2030 3 1)
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a R roll 29 February` (`ind-a copy` `an annual return of the charity` (YMD 2020 2 29)) `ind-a general company charity` EQUALS `the copy may be discarded on and after` (YMD 2030 3 2)
-- S8.6-04 a document 8(6) does not list -> no duty to retain (src:250-253)
#ASSERT `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` `ind-a R` (`ind-a copy` `a document of a kind that Article 8(6) does not list` (YMD 2020 3 15)) `ind-a general company charity` EQUALS `Article 8(6) does not require the copy to be retained`
-- S8.6-02 discarding on 2030-03-14 is within the retention period (a breach); discarding on 2030-03-16 is not
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` `ind-a R` (`ind-a copy` `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it` (YMD 2020 3 15)) `ind-a general company charity` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2020 3 15)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2030 3 14))
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` `ind-a R` (`ind-a copy` `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it` (YMD 2020 3 15)) `ind-a general company charity` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2020 3 15)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2030 3 16))

§§ `Article 9 (S9.1-01 to S9.7-03)`

-- S9.1-01 the registration number is public; the registered name is not (src:256)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `the registration number`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `the registered name`
-- S9.1-02 8(3)(a), (e), (f), (j), (k) are public (src:257)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `a note of the status of the entity`)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the registered charitable purposes`)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the registered public benefit statement`)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served`)
-- S9.1-03 8(3)(b), (c), (d), (g), (h), (i), (l), (m), (n) are not (src:255-259)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the names of each of the governors`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the principal address`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the address of any other premises in Jersey`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the date on which the charity was registered`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the previous registered names`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `other information prescribed by the Minister by Order`)
-- S9.1-04 the charity's summary of reasons, and an element an Order prescribes, are public (src:258-259)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `the summary of the reasons for registration, produced by the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `another element prescribed by an Order under Article 9(1)(d)`

GIVEN st IS A `Standing on the register`
      funding IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a may request` st funding other MEANS `Art 9(2) the request for entry in the restricted section may be made` `ind-a R` (`ind-a charity entity` st (LIST `a company`)) funding other

-- S9.2-01 an applicant meeting the funding condition -> may request (src:260-261)
#ASSERT `ind-a may request` `an applicant for registration` TRUE FALSE
-- S9.2-02 a general-section charity meeting another prescribed condition -> may request (src:260, src:262)
#ASSERT `ind-a may request` `entered in the general section` FALSE TRUE
-- S9.2-03 an applicant meeting no prescribed condition -> may not (src:260-262)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a may request` `an applicant for registration` FALSE FALSE
-- S9.2-04 already in the restricted section -> not a requester (src:260)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a may request` `entered in the restricted section` TRUE FALSE
-- S9.2-05 deregistered; neither applying nor registered -> not a requester (src:260)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a may request` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a may request` `not on the register` TRUE FALSE

GIVEN grounds IS A BOOLEAN, soliciting IS A BOOLEAN, donation IS A BOOLEAN, describes IS A BOOLEAN, publicDef IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Content of an Order under Article 9`
`ind-a 9 Order` grounds soliciting donation describes publicDef MEANS
    `Content of an Order under Article 9` WITH
        `prescribes grounds on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse a request` IS grounds
        `specifies what constitutes soliciting` IS soliciting
        `specifies what constitutes a donation` IS donation
        `prescribes a description of persons` IS describes
        `specifies what constitutes the general public` IS publicDef

-- S9.3-01 the Order must prescribe grounds and define soliciting, donation and (absent a description of persons) the general public (src:263-269)
#ASSERT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`ind-a 9 Order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`ind-a 9 Order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`ind-a 9 Order` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`ind-a 9 Order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`ind-a 9 Order` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

GIVEN form IS A BOOLEAN, evidence IS A BOOLEAN, intention IS A MAYBE `Intention stated with a request (Article 9(5))`
GIVETH A `Request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9)`
`ind-a request` form evidence intention MEANS
    `Request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9)` WITH
        `made in the form published by the Commissioner` IS form
        `supported by information and evidence to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` IS evidence
        `accompanied by a statement of the intention` IS intention

`ind-a applicant entity` MEANS `ind-a charity entity` `an applicant for registration` (LIST `a company`)
`ind-a general entity` MEANS `ind-a charity entity` `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`)

-- S9.4-01 published form, evidence to the Commissioner's satisfaction, a valid statement -> complied (src:270-279)
#ASSERT `Art 9(4) and (5) the request complied` `ind-a applicant entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE TRUE (JUST `that the application should be treated as withdrawn`))
-- S9.4-02 not in the published form -> fails 9(4)(a) (src:271)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(4) and (5) the request complied` `ind-a applicant entity` (`ind-a request` FALSE TRUE (JUST `that the application should be treated as withdrawn`))
-- S9.4-03 evidence not to the Commissioner's satisfaction -> fails 9(4)(b) (src:272)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(4) and (5) the request complied` `ind-a applicant entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE FALSE (JUST `that the application should be treated as withdrawn`))
-- S9.5-01 an applicant's two valid statements (src:274-276)
#ASSERT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `ind-a applicant entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE TRUE (JUST `that the application should be treated as withdrawn`))
#ASSERT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `ind-a applicant entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE TRUE (JUST `that the application should be treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required`))
-- S9.5-02 a general-section charity's two valid statements (src:277-279)
#ASSERT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `ind-a general entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE TRUE (JUST `that the charity should remain so registered`))
#ASSERT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `ind-a general entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE TRUE (JUST `that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required`))
-- S9.5-03 the statements crossed over -> not valid (src:273-279)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `ind-a applicant entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE TRUE (JUST `that the charity should remain so registered`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `ind-a general entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE TRUE (JUST `that the application should be treated as withdrawn`))
-- S9.5-04 no statement -> fails 9(5) (src:273)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `ind-a applicant entity` (`ind-a request` TRUE TRUE NOTHING)

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Satisfaction of the Commissioner under Article 9(6)`
`ind-a satisfied` a b c MEANS
    `Satisfaction of the Commissioner under Article 9(6)` WITH
        `satisfied that the request complied with paragraphs (4) and (5)` IS a
        `satisfied that one of the conditions prescribed under paragraph (2) is met` IS b
        `satisfied that there is no ground on which the request must be refused or, for a discretionary ground, should be refused` IS c

-- S9.6-01 all three satisfied -> may enter (src:280-283)
#ASSERT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`ind-a satisfied` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 9(6) the Commissioner must not enter the charity in the restricted section unless satisfied` (`ind-a satisfied` TRUE TRUE TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter a charity in the restricted section of the register` AT 1
-- S9.6-02 to S9.6-05 one satisfaction missing -> must not enter; entering is a breach
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`ind-a satisfied` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`ind-a satisfied` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`ind-a satisfied` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 9(6) the Commissioner must not enter the charity in the restricted section unless satisfied` (`ind-a satisfied` TRUE FALSE TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter a charity in the restricted section of the register` AT 1
-- S9.6-04, S9.6-05 a mandatory ground applies; a discretionary ground the Commissioner considers should lead to refusal -> (c) not met (src:283)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6)(c) there is no ground on which the request must be refused or should be refused` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6)(c) there is no ground on which the request must be refused or should be refused` FALSE TRUE
-- S9.6-06 a discretionary ground the Commissioner considers should not lead to refusal -> (c) met (src:283)
#ASSERT `Art 9(6)(c) there is no ground on which the request must be refused or should be refused` FALSE FALSE
-- S9.7-01 a refusal -> written notice owed; giving it discharges the duty (src:285)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 9(7)(a) the Commissioner must give written notice of the refusal` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give written notice of the refusal of a request` AT 1
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 9(7)(a) the Commissioner must give written notice of the refusal` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `establish and maintain a register of charities` AT 1
-- S9.7-02, S9.7-03 proceeding on the stated intention (src:286)
#ASSERT `Art 9(7)(b) the consequence of proceeding on the intention` `that the application should be treated as withdrawn` EQUALS `the application is treated as withdrawn`
#ASSERT `Art 9(7)(b) the consequence of proceeding on the intention` `that the application should be treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required` EQUALS `the application is treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required`
#ASSERT `Art 9(7)(b) the consequence of proceeding on the intention` `that the charity should remain so registered` EQUALS `the charity remains registered in the general section`
#ASSERT `Art 9(7)(b) the consequence of proceeding on the intention` `that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required` EQUALS `the charity is treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required`

§§ `Article 10 (S10.1-01 to S10.4-04)`

-- S10.1-01 the website duty is discharged by making the public parts available free (src:288)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 10(1) the Commissioner must make the public parts of the register available on a website` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `make the public parts of the register available to the public on a website for inspection without charge` AT 1

GIVEN other IS A BOOLEAN, charge IS A MAYBE `Charge for access to the public parts of the register (Article 10(2))`
GIVETH A `Content of an Order under Article 10(2)`
`ind-a 10(2) Order` other charge MEANS `Content of an Order under Article 10(2)` WITH `specifies another manner in which the public parts are made available` IS other, `payment required` IS charge

-- S10.2-01 another manner on payment of a specified charge, or of a charge the Commissioner determines and publishes -> within 10(2) (src:289-291)
#ASSERT `Art 10(2) the Order provides for another specified manner of access on payment of a charge within (a) or (b)` (`ind-a 10(2) Order` TRUE (JUST `a specified charge`))
#ASSERT `Art 10(2) the Order provides for another specified manner of access on payment of a charge within (a) or (b)` (`ind-a 10(2) Order` TRUE (JUST `a charge determined and published by the Commissioner`))

GIVEN st IS A `Standing on the register`
      m IS A `Matter entered on the register`
      designated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a public` st m designated MEANS `Art 10(3) the matter is in a public part of the register` `ind-a R` (`ind-a charity entity` st (LIST `a company`)) m designated

-- S10.3-01 governor names of a general-section charity -> public (src:293)
#ASSERT `ind-a public` `entered in the general section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the names of each of the governors`) FALSE
-- S10.3-02 purposes of a restricted charity -> public; its governor names -> not (src:294)
#ASSERT `ind-a public` `entered in the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the registered charitable purposes`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a public` `entered in the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the names of each of the governors`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a public` `entered in the restricted section` `the registered name` FALSE
-- S10.3-03 a historic section entry -> public (src:295)
#ASSERT `ind-a public` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` (`an item required by Article 8(5)` `the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered`) FALSE
-- S10.4-01 the Commissioner considers a significant risk to safety from access to a refuge's address -> 10(5) applies; once designated, not public (src:296-297)
#ASSERT `Art 10(4) paragraph (5) applies` `ind-a R` `ind-a general entity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a public` `entered in the general section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the principal address`) TRUE
-- S10.4-02 no significant risk in the Commissioner's view -> 10(5) does not apply (src:296)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(4) paragraph (5) applies` `ind-a R` `ind-a general entity` FALSE
-- S10.4-03 risk, but no designation -> still public (src:297)
#ASSERT `ind-a public` `entered in the general section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the principal address`) FALSE
-- S10.4-04 a historic-section entry (AMBIG-9), my literal reading -> no designation power
#ASSERT NOT `Art 10(4) paragraph (5) applies` `ind-a R` (`ind-a charity entity` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` (LIST `a company`)) TRUE
